# tools/h/hitmiss_witness.rish -- the hit-or-miss transform proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the exact-configuration detector the general structuring element opens. Where
# image/structure.rye reshapes a mask by any offset set, the hit-or-miss transform asks a sharper question: does the
# FOREGROUND template fit the shape HERE and the BACKGROUND template fit the ground THERE at once? It is the floor thinning,
# skeletonization, and corner / endpoint / junction detection descend from -- each is a hit-or-miss with a chosen pair of
# templates.
#
# The crux this witness proves is the classic composition run on metal: hit_or_miss = erode(A, fg) AND erode(complement(A),
# bg), leaning on structure.erode_se for both fits. An isolated-point detector (fg the center, bg the eight neighbors)
# lights a lone white dot and nothing else; when fg and bg share a cell the disjointness law leaves the result empty (no
# pixel is both shape and ground); a background cell genuinely requires ground, so a solid field matches nothing; the output
# is always opaque white-on-black even from a translucent source (the plane pins alpha, sidestepping the complement trap); a
# mid-gray at or above 128 reads as shape and below it as ground; the result round-trips through the open QOI codec
# byte-for-byte; an empty foreground, an empty background, an over-max template, and an empty source refuse by name;
# the same match is deterministic. No network, no key, no funds -- the endpoint, the corner, and the junction a surface
# detects the day it thins a mask to its skeleton, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/h/hitmiss_witness.rish

say "hitmiss: Language EN -- Season G hit-or-miss transform; mark every pixel where a foreground template fits the shape and a disjoint background template fits the ground, the exact-configuration detector the general structuring element opens."
say "hitmiss: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the binarize and the final AND; structure.erode_se owns the fit gather; the isolated-point detector lights a lone dot and nothing else; disjoint templates leave the result empty."
say "hitmiss: Lens TAME -- u8 threshold decides foreground once; the source and both templates guarded and refused by name up front so a refusal allocates nothing; the plane pins alpha opaque so the complement never turns a solid mask transparent; the AND is a per-channel min (a rank of bytes is a byte) so nothing wraps; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/hitmiss"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/hitmiss.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hitmiss: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hitmiss: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "hitmiss: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-hitmiss" else "hitmiss: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "hitmiss: GREEN -- the hit-or-miss transform detects an exact local pattern, the isolated point lit and the block left dark, the disjointness law holding, the output opaque, on metal."
